{
  "slug": "artist:nas",
  "name": "Nas",
  "editorial_article": "Nas, born Nasir bin Olu Dara Jones in 1973, began his career in 1991 with a guest performance on the Main Source track \"Live at the Barbeque.\" His 1994 debut studio album, Illmatic, released on Columbia Records, remains a critical cornerstone of East Coast hip hop. He later achieved mainstream reach with his 1996 sophomore album, It Was Written, which featured the Lauryn Hill collaboration \"If I Ruled the World (Imagine That).\" In the 2020s, Nas entered a prolific period, releasing the King's Disease trilogy produced by Hit-Boy, with the first installment arriving in August 2020. Over his career, he has explored collaborative projects, notably forming the group The Firm with AZ, Cormega, Foxy Brown, and Nature in 1997, and releasing the 2010 album Distant Relatives with Damian Marley.",
